    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (66.99) serving as our clear offensive anchor. Facing Landen Roupp, **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a favorable SP_xERA of 4.07 and a solid spot in the order, making him our only truly \"Strong\" play of the day. **Andy Pages** (57.86) also projects well against Roupp, as his middle-of-the-order positioning allows him to capitalize on run-production opportunities despite the slight drag caused by catcher pop-times. Meanwhile, the middle infield core\u2014specifically **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (55.84)\u2014receives a significant boost from a dynamic platoon advantage against Corbin Burnes. While Burnes is an elite arm, the optimizer rewards **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** for his ability to handle right-handed velocity, pushing his score well above his base projection.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Sam Antonacci** (48.56) and **Liam Hicks** (50.18). **Sam Antonacci** carries an elite 0.403 xwOBA, but his L/L platoon disadvantage against Kris Bubic ultimately suppressed his ceiling, keeping him just behind the production floor of **Liam Hicks**. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all players, as any downward shift in batting order for **Nasim Nunez** or **Dominic Smith**\u2014already sitting at marginal scores of 40.76 and 41.72\u2014could trigger a defensive swap to preserve game caps.\n\nWe remain shorthanded as we wait for **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** to return from the IL, and with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** off the schedule today, our depth is being tested. We are particularly cautious regarding the matchups for **Brady House** and **Nasim Nunez** against Burnes; while we are starting them to maintain our stolen base profile, the risk of a low-scoring performance against an elite SP_xERA is non-negligible. We advise keeping a close watch on the official lineups for **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin** to ensure our catcher slot efficiency remains intact.",
